From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:47:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/smmstore: Let the payload end the full flash access

On a boot that starts with update capsules, the SMMSTORE handler serves
the whole flash until the next boot, and the payload has to reboot
before anything else can reach it. A capsule on disk, though, is only
announced by a bit in OsIndications: the payload may find no capsule
file, or have to postpone the update for a low battery, and then reboots
for nothing; and if coreboot and the payload read that variable
differently, the payload doesn't know it has to reboot at all.

Once the full flash is enabled, let SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH with a
zero argument disable it until the next boot, so that the payload can
give it up and boot on when it has written nothing. The handler only
loses access with it.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 Documentation/drivers/smmstore.md | 20 +++++++++++---------
 src/drivers/smmstore/store.c      |  5 +++++
 src/include/smmstore.h            |  3 ++-
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/drivers/smmstore.md b/Documentation/drivers/smmstore.md
index a647ecb86..63dde2249 100644
--- a/Documentation/drivers/smmstore.md
+++ b/Documentation/drivers/smmstore.md
@@ -241,19 +241,21 @@ with highest bit set can be used.
 
 ### - SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH = 0x80
 
-This command can only be executed once and is done by the firmware.
-Calling this function at runtime has no effect. It takes one additional
-parameter that, contrary to other commands, isn't a pointer. Instead,
-`%ebx` indicates requested state of full flash access. If it equals 0,
-commands for accessing full flash are permanently disabled, otherwise
-they are permanently enabled until the next boot.
+This command is executed by the firmware, which decides whether the boot
+gets full flash access. It takes one additional parameter that, contrary
+to other commands, isn't a pointer. Instead, `%ebx` indicates requested
+state of full flash access. If it equals 0, commands for accessing full
+flash are permanently disabled, otherwise they are enabled until the next
+boot. Once they are enabled, calling it again with 0 disables them until
+the next boot; any other later call has no effect.
 
 The assumption is that if capsule updates are enabled at build time and
 whole flash access is enabled at runtime, a UEFI payload (highly likely
 EDK2 or its derivative) won't allow a regular OS to boot if the handler is
-enabled without rebooting first. There could be a way of deactivating the
-handler, but coreboot, having no way of enforcing its usage, might as well
-permit access until a reboot and rely on the payload to do the right thing.
+enabled without rebooting first. The payload either reboots or, when it
+has written nothing (no capsule found, or the update postponed), disables
+the access and goes on booting. coreboot, having no way of enforcing it,
+relies on the payload to do the right thing.
 
 ## External links
 
diff --git a/src/drivers/smmstore/store.c b/src/drivers/smmstore/store.c
index e950a4239..b5715200a 100644
--- a/src/drivers/smmstore/store.c
+++ b/src/drivers/smmstore/store.c
@@ -37,6 +37,11 @@ int smmstore_preprocess_cmd(uint8_t *cmd, void *param)
 			 * the caller whether capsule handling was enabled or not.
 			 */
 			return has_capsules;
+		} else if (has_capsules == 1 && *cmd == SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH && !param) {
+			/* The payload is done with the capsules: no full flash until reboot */
+			has_capsules = 0;
+			smmstore_use_full_flash = 0;
+			return 1;
 		} else if (has_capsules == 1 && *cmd & SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH) {
 			smmstore_use_full_flash = 1;
 			*cmd &= ~SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH;
diff --git a/src/include/smmstore.h b/src/include/smmstore.h
index 8962137db..6b25774cb 100644
--- a/src/include/smmstore.h
+++ b/src/include/smmstore.h
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@
  * Availability depends on CONFIG(DRIVERS_EFI_UPDATE_CAPSULES). Usage of this
  * extension requires considering which portions of the flash is read-only or
  * otherwise protected to avoid causing problems while trying to overwrite
- * them.
+ * them. As a standalone command with a zero argument, after the firmware has
+ * enabled the full flash, it disables it until the next boot.
  */
 #define SMMSTORE_CMD_USE_FULL_FLASH 0x80
 
